-- 145: ALL THIRTEEN — every layer on a 13 grid, half-time, sample-based voices.
-- Started as three co-prime metres (13/17/23) drifting against each other; the
-- operator's call was "everything should be in 13", so 17 and 23 are gone and
-- EVERY pattern is a 13-division (euclids, slice counts and order sequences).
-- The drift now comes from different ROTATIONS of 13 (offsets like (2,13,6),
-- (3,13,3), (7,13)) rather than from coprime periods — the same metre displaced,
-- which reads as polyrhythm against the downbeat without ever fighting it.
--   13 everywhere: kick (4,13); snare <(2,13,6) (1,13) (3,13) (2,13)>; hats
--      <(5,13) (3,13) (7,13) (2,13)>; claps <(3,13,3) (2,13,7) (5,13)>; accent
--      ho(1,13); click <(3,13) (2,13) (5,13)>; break + drum loops sliced into 13
--      with 13-slot orders; vocal fragments (1,13,5).
-- The earlier snare was the annoyance: three overlapping euclids (3,5,2,4 hits)
-- x every 3 (iter 2) x sometimesBy (fast 2) = 5-8 snare hits a cycle, sprayed
-- evenly across the bar. Now two hits a cycle at most, offset.
-- Melody (d6) — RHCP "Under the Bridge" (1991) verse line from ~/tunepile; the
--   whole line is F# minor (gs fs e cs, no accidentals). Mars DX100_Marimba at
--   n 0. For SAMPLE melodies `note` IS playback speed: keep the line above ~fs4
--   (gs3/fs3 dragged the sample to molasses) and do not jump an octave up
--   (`|+ note 12` = 2x speed = the squeak).
-- Chords (d9) — mars_synths_OB_Strings, an 8-chord progression over 32 cycles
--   (~55 s): F#m D Bm C#m / A E Bm C#m, voiced above middle C (fs4/cs5/a5 — the
--   first voicing was far too deep; one octave higher thinned the sample out
--   because a sampled pad at 2x speed loses its body). The ONLY wet element:
--   verbSend 0.55, room 0.8, size 0.9, verbT60 6.
-- Drums (d5, d11-d13) — real drum loops, see LOOPS.md for the pNN alias map:
--   p93drumB = "300 breaks/12", p94brkB a Funky break, p93drumA the breaklots
--   loop played whole. These replaced lpmr/lpviz for the cutups: those packs are
--   the WHOLE loopmaster libraries (vocals and FX included) indexed only by n, so
--   `n (choose [...])` sometimes drew a vocal loop — the "mousey" squeak.
-- Vocal feels (d14) — lpviz 169-200 are 2020_DD_Vox1..32. Fragments are taken
--   with begin/end at speed 1 (natural pitch, no squeak), gated on 1-in-13 with an
--   occasional fast-2 double so they are INFREQUENT, and sent to a SMALL amount of space
--   (verbSend 0.18, room 0.35, size 0.45 + dub delay 0.22 @3/16 — the earlier
--   0.42/0.6/0.75 + 0.45 delay was overwhelming). begin/end are paired patterns so the window cannot
--   invert. NOTE: sometimesBy is a pattern transform, so it wraps the pattern
--   (`sometimesBy 0.3 (fast 2) $ s ...`) — it is NOT a `# param`.
-- The sub (d4) is SILENCED: the bassline was carrying too much weight and mud;
--   d6 melody hpf raised to 420 to take its low body out, and the drum loops
--   damped (gains down, hpf 160-220, lpf ~5500) because their toms hit hard.
-- Rules that keep biting (also in LOOPS.md):
--   * `speed`  = playback rate (pitch follows), keeps slice-to-cycle mapping.
--   * `loopAt N`>1 = fits the loop over N cycles, i.e. speed/N and N octaves-ish
--     down — `loopAt 4` is the "insanely slowed" sound. Use deliberately.
--   * `slow N` = stretches event timing only, no pitch change.
--   * `begin`/`end` = window inside the buffer; play at speed 1 for real pitch.
-- Mix: master mHpf 48 / mCut 11000 / mGain 0.85. Three sub-ish layers stacked
--   badly once (sub + Micro_Sub impacts + low kick) so the low end is: one sub
--   (hpf 34), kick hpf 46, no second sub layer. All group aux sends are 0
--   (drums/bass/music/fx) so nothing hits the project verb/shimmer buses.
setcps 0.5833

d1 $ s "808bd(4,13)" # gain 0.95 # shape 0.5 # hpf 46 # release 0.09 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d2 $ every 3 (iter 2) $ sometimesBy 0.25 (fast 2) $ s "<sn(2,13,6) sn(1,13) sn(3,13) sn(2,13)>" # gain 0.78 # hpf 420 # shape 0.4 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d3 $ s "<hh(5,13) ho(3,13) hh(7,13) ho(2,13)>" # gain 0.5 # hpf 1800 # lpf 12000 # pan 0.6 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d4 $ silence

d5 $ every 4 (rev) $ loopAt 1 $ slice 13 "<[0 ~ 4 ~ 8 ~ 12 ~] [12 ~ 8 ~ 4 ~ 0 ~] [0 ~ 6 ~ 12 ~ 5 ~] [8 ~ 3 ~ 11 ~ 6 ~]>" $ s "breaks165" # gain 0.6 # hpf 250 # lpf 5500 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d6 $ slow 4 $ note "<[gs4 ~ gs4 fs4 ~ e4 e4 cs4 ~ e4 cs4 fs4 e4 ~ gs4 ~] [gs4 ~ fs4 e4 ~ cs4 e4 cs4 fs4 ~ e4 gs4 fs4 gs4 ~ ~] [gs4 fs4 gs4 e4 ~ gs4 cs4 e4 ~ cs4 fs4 e4 ~ e4 ~ ~] [gs4 ~ gs4 fs4 e4 ~ cs4 ~ e4 cs4 fs4 ~ e4 e4 gs4 ~]>" # s "mars_synths_DX100_Marimba" # n 0 # gain 0.75 # hpf 420 # lpf 9000 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d7 $ s "ho(1,13)" # gain 0.42 # hpf 2600 # pan 0.5 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d8 $ s "<cp(3,13,3) cp(2,13,7) cp(5,13)>" # gain 0.5 # hpf 750 # lpf 7200 # speed 1.1 # release 0.09 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d9 $ slow 4 $ note "<[fs4,cs5,a5] [d4,a4,fs5] [b3,fs4,d5] [cs4,gs4,e5] [a3,e4,cs5] [e4,b4,gs5] [b3,fs4,d5] [cs4,gs4,e5]>" # s "mars_synths_OB_Strings" # n 0 # gain 0.7 # hpf 280 # lpf 6500 # attack 0.06 # release 1.2 # verbSend 0.55 # room 0.8 # size 0.9 # verbT60 6 # verbDamp 0.4 # ddSend 0

d10 $ s "<ho(3,13) hh(2,13) ho(5,13)>" # gain 0.4 # hpf 2600 # pan 0.45 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d11 $ loopAt 1 $ slice 13 "<[0 ~ 5 ~ 10 ~ 2 ~ 7 ~ 12 ~] [12 ~ 9 ~ 6 ~ 3 ~ 0 ~ 10 ~] [0 ~ ~ 3 ~ ~ 7 ~ ~ 11 ~ ~ ~] [4 ~ 6 ~ 8 ~ 10 ~ 12 ~ 0 ~]>" $ s "p93drumB" # speed 0.9 # gain 0.42 # hpf 160 # lpf 5500 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d12 $ sometimesBy 0.3 (fast 2) $ loopAt 1 $ slice 13 "<[12 ~ 9 ~ 6 ~ 3 ~ 0 ~ 10 ~] [2 ~ 5 ~ 8 ~ 11 ~ 1 ~ 4 ~] [12 ~ ~ 9 ~ ~ 6 ~ ~ 3 ~ ~ ~] [6 ~ 5 ~ 4 ~ 3 ~ 2 ~ 1 ~]>" $ s "p94brkB" # speed 0.95 # gain 0.38 # hpf 200 # lpf 5200 # pan 0.4 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d13 $ silence

d14 $ sometimesBy 0.3 (fast 2) $ s "lpviz(1,13,5)" # n (slow 8 $ choose [169,170,175,180,186,192]) # begin "<0.05 0.30 0.55 0.75>" # end "<0.20 0.45 0.70 0.95>" # speed 1 # gain 0.62 # hpf 320 # lpf 7000 # pan 0.55 # verbSend 0.18 # room 0.35 # size 0.45 # ddSend 0.22 # lock 1 # delaytime (3/16) # delayfeedback 0.18
